            {
                "entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                "word": "responsabilisation",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "82c7e65c-14bc-494e-b52c-47beea9fa500",
                        "entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "responsabilisations"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "e71ec1bf-7a90-3254-bb54-0f1e5f3f3bfd",
                        "entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Action de rendre responsable, action de responsabiliser"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "220a2fba-c0ac-41c2-a152-3bcbfafcd1a7",
                                "sense_id": "e71ec1bf-7a90-3254-bb54-0f1e5f3f3bfd",
                                "text": "Le premier ministre en a aussi appelé à la responsabilisation des citoyens, en s’adressent notamment à ceux de la grande région de Montréal qui choisissent de s’évader à Saint-Sauveur pour aller manger au restaurant."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ba639cee-770c-4fa4-8485-573c6ee21961",
                                "sense_id": "e71ec1bf-7a90-3254-bb54-0f1e5f3f3bfd",
                                "text": "Toutefois, il faut en appeler à la responsabilisation de chacun, et dans la région, on a des collaborateurs de la Sûreté du Québec qui sont prêts au cas où l'on aurait des situations qui représenteraient un risque pour la santé des gens."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6f45ffe3-9dac-395c-89b5-2cd5a85f0184",
                        "entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Principe donnant plus de flexibilité à une personne tout en imposant une obligation de résultat et de justification."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "Gestion"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2598239c-52a7-4b70-b9a7-a3aceda66353",
                                "sense_id": "6f45ffe3-9dac-395c-89b5-2cd5a85f0184",
                                "text": "Le précepte majeur de Régis Le Bris à la tête du centre de formation des Merlus tient dans la responsabilisation des jeunes joueurs."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f77572a6-38d1-4d82-9106-14ad0d062c3f",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                        "source_sense_description": "action de responsabiliser",
                        "target_lang_word": "responsibilization",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "responsibilization",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1a2f7c41-b89c-3162-86bb-0f5a603cb5ad",
                                        "entry_id": "f60ef677-c338-3db0-93c0-c2b33fa2ae8e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The transfer of responsibility from higher authorities to communities or individuals who are then called on to take an active role in resolving their own problems."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b7049ea5-eb08-411d-b740-25443024b2f3",
                                                "sense_id": "1a2f7c41-b89c-3162-86bb-0f5a603cb5ad",
                                                "text": "Responsibilization strategies involve a series of new techniques and methods \"whereby the state seeks to bring about action on the part of private agencies and individuals - either by stimulating new forms of behaviour or by stopping established habits\" (emphasis in the original)."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "1cf6996f-6001-4da9-a182-4ef8a674ccdb",
                                                "sense_id": "1a2f7c41-b89c-3162-86bb-0f5a603cb5ad",
                                                "text": "While responsibilization has become closely associated with neo-liberalism, with its inducement that individuals become entrepreneurs, it should be noted that responsibilization played a significant role in other historical periods."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "dbd18d02-b416-4764-97c1-2166d1e33ea6",
                                                "sense_id": "1a2f7c41-b89c-3162-86bb-0f5a603cb5ad",
                                                "text": "Responsibilization is not an inherent entailment of devolution; there are decidedly more empowering and more democratic potentials for devolved decision making."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "864a000c-5bcb-4793-a821-68a1d08c37bf",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                        "source_sense_description": "action de responsabiliser",
                        "target_lang_word": "responsabilizzazione",
                        "target_lang_code": "it",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "responsabilizzazione",
                                "target_lang_code": "it",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5ff680bd-492d-3140-903e-41731e17ee0a",
                                        "entry_id": "80a31d08-2946-3442-81e5-b22d1af2ce9c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "assegnazione di responsabilità a qualcuno"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "diritto"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "776e0e17-4832-432e-bf3f-5034bc5049a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "b0ff272f-5e1c-3db2-a2d3-f6a1eef84b76",
                        "source_sense_description": "principe de gestion",
                        "target_lang_word": "accountability",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "accountability",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "86c307d2-174b-3b46-8158-32224b0acab8",
                                        "entry_id": "71157bf9-38c1-359f-8898-f6c6966c2278",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being accountable; liability to be called on to render an account or give an explanation; liability to be held responsible or answerable for something."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0d56ff1c-82d7-480a-bc37-21bf1a80cd57",
                                                "sense_id": "86c307d2-174b-3b46-8158-32224b0acab8",
                                                "text": "The United States stands at this time at the pinnacle of world power. It is a solemn moment for the American Democracy. For with primacy in power is also joined an awe-inspiring accountability to the future."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c2d73619-d089-3033-8093-a99720c84b48",
                                        "entry_id": "71157bf9-38c1-359f-8898-f6c6966c2278",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An open determination of one's responsibility for something and imposition of consequences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2e5f063d-766a-474f-a27c-8b9f12da0e80",
                                                "sense_id": "c2d73619-d089-3033-8093-a99720c84b48",
                                                "text": "Just think about that: 1 in 4 had an error, and 1 in 20 was seriously wrong. And that is not good. If every 20th Frosty that Wendy’s sold turned out to be a cup of warm goat semen, we would want some accountability and we’d want it fast! At least freeze it!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7b9fbaee-b4a9-46d7-b588-128a04e5647d",
                                                "sense_id": "c2d73619-d089-3033-8093-a99720c84b48",
                                                "text": "Levying a charge will not, by itself, guarantee accountability: witness the millions of dissatisfied customers of the private sector travel agents who book the wrong holiday, solicitors who over-charge, builders who do shoddy work, garages that misrepair cars, estate agents who mislead, shops that sell defective goods and refuse refunds, etc."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "39607b5f-9eb9-37c4-80db-b4a4aa2d49d1",
                                        "entry_id": "71157bf9-38c1-359f-8898-f6c6966c2278",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An acceptance of good faith of one's responsibility for something and of its consequences."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cd13dc72-612f-42d8-8402-0735800c65ec",
                                                "sense_id": "39607b5f-9eb9-37c4-80db-b4a4aa2d49d1",
                                                "text": "As the biggest rail player, Network Rail was usually held accountable for failings, but had no authority to change anything to solve the problems. The DfT had been given that authority in 2004 - but consistently ducked accountability."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77f541a5-f03b-4dcd-9077-3a58ea0e7865",
                                                "sense_id": "39607b5f-9eb9-37c4-80db-b4a4aa2d49d1",
                                                "text": "The erosion of accountability doesn't seem to matter now, but it will matter when things start unraveling."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dc298e9c-02e9-363a-98d7-120c767c16ec",
                                        "entry_id": "71157bf9-38c1-359f-8898-f6c6966c2278",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The obligation imposed by law or regulation on an officer or other person for keeping an accurate record of property, documents, or funds."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
